<!--
  The catalog's weekly check on the owner's Mac (docs/plans/indexer-catalog-upkeep.md, part B).
  `bun run catalog:check schedule` fills in the paths and installs it as a per-user agent in
  ~/Library/LaunchAgents; `bun run catalog:check unschedule` removes it. Never install it by hand
  with these placeholders.

  From Apple's documentation:
  - A per-user agent lives in ~/Library/LaunchAgents and runs as that user (launchd.plist(5)).
  - StartCalendarInterval runs it at a time of the week, like crontab(5); Weekday 1 is Monday.
    "Unlike cron which skips job invocations when the computer is asleep, launchd will start the
    job the next time the computer wakes up. If multiple intervals transpire before the computer
    is woken, those events will be coalesced into one event upon wake from sleep." (launchd.plist(5);
    Scheduling Timed Jobs, https://developer.apple.com/library/archive/documentation/MacOSX/Conceptual/BPSystemStartup/Chapters/ScheduledJobs.html)
  - launchd gives a job no shell profile, so the PATH (for gh and git) is set here, and the
    program is the absolute path of bun (Creating Launch Daemons and Agents,
    https://developer.apple.com/library/archive/documentation/MacOSX/Conceptual/BPSystemStartup/Chapters/CreatingLaunchdJobs.html).
  - `launchctl bootstrap gui/<uid>` loads it and `launchctl bootout` unloads it; launchctl(1)
    recommends them over the older load and unload.

  The third program argument, the github switch, keeps the "Catalog check" issue up to date with
  the owner's own gh; take it out of ProgramArguments to keep the run on this Mac only.
-->
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>tv.highsea.catalog-check</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>__BUN__</string>
    <string>scripts/catalog-check.ts</string>
    <string>--github</string>
  </array>
  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>__REPO__</string>
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PATH</key>
    <string>__PATH__</string>
  </dict>
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <dict>
    <key>Weekday</key>
    <integer>1</integer>
    <key>Hour</key>
    <integer>9</integer>
    <key>Minute</key>
    <integer>0</integer>
  </dict>
  <key>ProcessType</key>
  <string>Background</string>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>__LOG__</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>__LOG__</string>
</dict>
</plist>
